WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:02.450
A manager gets funding for one navigator and

2
00:00:02.450 --> 00:00:04.650
wants them to help any family, in any

3
00:00:04.650 --> 00:00:05.750
language, at any step.

4
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:06.760
What's the problem?

5
00:00:07.570 --> 00:00:09.050
One person can't do that.

6
00:00:09.320 --> 00:00:11.608
They'd be spread so thin you'd never see

7
00:00:11.608 --> 00:00:12.180
a difference.

8
00:00:12.890 --> 00:00:14.250
And the evidence points the other way.

9
00:00:14.560 --> 00:00:16.693
Navigation tends to help most when it's tied

10
00:00:16.693 --> 00:00:17.760
to a specific step.

11
00:00:18.070 --> 00:00:20.734
A 2021 trial of family navigation for autism

12
00:00:20.734 --> 00:00:23.399
found more families got a diagnostic answer within

13
00:00:23.399 --> 00:00:25.730
a year, though results varied by clinic.

14
00:00:26.060 --> 00:00:28.385
So start by finding where people get lost

15
00:00:28.385 --> 00:00:30.420
in your own process, and focus there.

16
00:00:30.990 --> 00:00:32.430
Then you write the job.

17
00:00:33.040 --> 00:00:35.056
Write the duties, and write what the role

18
00:00:35.056 --> 00:00:35.560
is not.

19
00:00:35.830 --> 00:00:39.190
The C3 Project's list of community health worker

20
00:00:39.190 --> 00:00:42.550
roles is a good menu: cultural mediation, system

21
00:00:42.550 --> 00:00:43.810
navigation, advocacy, outreach.

22
00:00:44.300 --> 00:00:45.900
And the not list matters just as much.

23
00:00:46.290 --> 00:00:48.706
Not an interpreter unless they're qualified and hired

24
00:00:48.706 --> 00:00:49.310
for it.

25
00:00:49.480 --> 00:00:50.320
Not a decision maker.

26
00:00:50.670 --> 00:00:52.170
Not overflow case management.

27
00:00:52.880 --> 00:00:53.940
Here's the one I see.

28
00:00:54.230 --> 00:00:56.350
No budget, so we ask our bilingual staff

29
00:00:56.350 --> 00:00:58.470
to just come along on a few visits.

30
00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:00.700
That's navigation without the job.

31
00:01:00.990 --> 00:01:03.434
It's unpaid, nobody counts it, and it can

32
00:01:03.434 --> 00:01:05.879
leave that person caught between their community and

33
00:01:05.879 --> 00:01:06.490
their work.

34
00:01:06.660 --> 00:01:08.482
Name it, count it, and either make it

35
00:01:08.482 --> 00:01:10.304
part of a recognized role or move it

36
00:01:10.304 --> 00:01:10.760
to one.

37
00:01:11.350 --> 00:01:14.257
Should the navigator work for the agency, or

38
00:01:14.257 --> 00:01:15.710
for a community organization?

39
00:01:16.520 --> 00:01:17.180
Both can work.

40
00:01:17.470 --> 00:01:19.770
Inside, you get easier access to systems.

41
00:01:20.180 --> 00:01:22.580
Through a community partner, you often get deeper

42
00:01:22.580 --> 00:01:22.880
trust.

43
00:01:23.290 --> 00:01:25.960
M Health Fairview's cultural brokers, for example, spend

44
00:01:25.960 --> 00:01:28.630
most of their time at trusted community organizations.

45
00:01:29.500 --> 00:01:30.600
And once they're hired?

46
00:01:31.230 --> 00:01:33.330
Supervise both sides of the work.

47
00:01:33.620 --> 00:01:36.157
Keep navigators out of enforcement and bad-news roles,

48
00:01:36.157 --> 00:01:38.060
so they keep the community's trust.

49
00:01:38.410 --> 00:01:41.059
And plan caseloads with secondary traumatic stress in

50
00:01:41.059 --> 00:01:41.390
mind.

51
00:01:41.760 --> 00:01:43.840
Hearing hard stories every day has a cost.

52
00:01:44.530 --> 00:01:48.035
A clear purpose, a written scope, fair pay

53
00:01:48.035 --> 00:01:49.350
and real support.

54
00:01:49.640 --> 00:01:51.780
A role, not a favor.
